      </div>
      <div class="ed-beliefs__copy">
        <p>Security only works when the architecture actually survives contact with a <em>live adversary</em>. Building resilient systems means tracking behavioral tradecraft instead of just chasing indicators, while treating trust as something that must be earned continuously. A network will only hold up under pressure if the environment remains <em>completely legible</em>.</p>
        <p>Ultimately, this profession is just figuring out how things break and engineering them to be much harder to crack. I have always loved that part.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
